/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-10143"] :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡(7x)\\operatorname{tan}⁡(7x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "If we let $u=7x,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=7\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{7}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡(7x)\\operatorname{tan}⁡(7x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡u\\operatorname{tan}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{7}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡u\\operatorname{tan}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\operatorname{sec}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(7x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-13663/selection/e121e1be7ed55ae228c69b78becff24007b0f53f078ee17a8e112e4b90db6306" :answer/id #uuid "d2548ff1-f212-5f1c-8087-7bfec03ec5cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-13663/selection/05402db46107d70ece210f0bd5e24b332ae4f43bd474d592035c3e3c92625629" :answer/id #uuid "dc81baf3-eeb4-5370-9bff-9075c8a7c9cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-13663/selection/4dc93382ae538a085a91852492f53a403a57d49793116fa5aa147b95dcf7c117" :answer/id #uuid "679e8ca2-40fa-5082-8beb-c046a0cf351a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-13663/selection/a05724295bc0340162295da21b8749cd336584b7c76ed9f6810ddb03e7f98d00" :answer/id #uuid "6cc6d654-89ef-57e5-92ab-b26afdf5de4c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-13663/selection/ac9362c9c743a0d4cd03c825418c9d77629147a5815c12295606faadbe8a8744" :answer/id #uuid "29701423-b2aa-5699-82fb-4786d80eab5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-13663/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "cc1beb27-57db-57d5-b791-b15ec816b98c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-13663/selection/e121e1be7ed55ae228c69b78becff24007b0f53f078ee17a8e112e4b90db6306" :answer-field/choices ["q-13663/selection/e121e1be7ed55ae228c69b78becff24007b0f53f078ee17a8e112e4b90db6306" "q-13663/selection/05402db46107d70ece210f0bd5e24b332ae4f43bd474d592035c3e3c92625629" "q-13663/selection/4dc93382ae538a085a91852492f53a403a57d49793116fa5aa147b95dcf7c117" "q-13663/selection/a05724295bc0340162295da21b8749cd336584b7c76ed9f6810ddb03e7f98d00" "q-13663/selection/ac9362c9c743a0d4cd03c825418c9d77629147a5815c12295606faadbe8a8744"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-13663" :question/id #uuid "a871d0b5-61bc-5e1e-9eae-078640c38be3" :question/math-academy-id "q-13663" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{\\pi /9}^{\\pi /6}2{csc}^{2}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "If we let $u=3x,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $\\pi /9$ | $\\pi /6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\pi /3$ | $\\pi /2$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /9}^{\\pi /6}2{csc}^{2}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}2{csc}^{2}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}{csc}^{2}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{cot}⁡u{|}_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}(\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}(0-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-13663/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "084eb4cc-2f84-5288-90a6-be84066922b6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-13663"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-13537/selection/3224ab5f6f5fb64621a714f7654c4df06661a69e7edb8f5993dcef1e46ce3dea" :answer/id #uuid "5003d46a-4c07-55ed-81e6-1fe92b31e728" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-13537/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "49906863-b9b5-5885-98a4-f424e1731eb5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-13537/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "bfb54050-161e-54f4-85de-0f3b0e5fedbd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-13537/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" :answer/id #uuid "f2cf6ba7-e39c-53ad-9ce8-4e022b373d73" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-13537/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "22627ab3-b26b-5ab6-9893-12f520e8e17f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-13537/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2b4436a3-16dd-5c6a-8e90-41a53f89f92f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-13537/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-13537/selection/3224ab5f6f5fb64621a714f7654c4df06661a69e7edb8f5993dcef1e46ce3dea" "q-13537/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-13537/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-13537/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" "q-13537/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-13537" :question/id #uuid "032f8bbb-4601-5ae2-a6a7-ea4ff94f6117" :question/math-academy-id "q-13537" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\pi }}3x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=2{x}^{2}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4x\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u=x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt{\\pi }$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $2\\pi $ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\pi }}3x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\pi }}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2{x}^{2})\\cdot x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }3\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u{|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}(1-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-13537/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d359337c-4ec2-5100-bdac-d0858619db3b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-13537"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-350202/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "7f83e2e9-56f5-5e87-bae4-67fa3bcbda49" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-350202/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "56b4a97d-170f-5c2a-afcd-ba87ae15bf2b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-350202/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "d909989c-8c22-5cd7-bb2e-44221f212a7f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-350202/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-350202/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-350202/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-350202" :question/id #uuid "46354ead-6195-554d-865f-0c30a629d69a" :question/math-academy-id "q-350202" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\pi /12}}8xsec\\,(4{x}^{2})tan\\,(4{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we let $u=4{x}^{2},$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=8x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=8x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt{\\pi /12}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\pi /3$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can rewrite the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\pi /12}}8xsec\\,(4{x}^{2})tan\\,(4{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\pi /12}}sec\\,(4{x}^{2})tan\\,(4{x}^{2})\\cdot 8x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(u)\\operatorname{tan}⁡(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡(u)\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{sec}⁡(0) \\\\  & =2-1 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-350202/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d359337c-4ec2-5100-bdac-d0858619db3b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-350202"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-13464/selection/745652f4c7afdd0c761deb3804adc7fde54e58f1dc166529b70f3c1c015c1c27" :answer/id #uuid "d8e3db1d-de75-53bc-a357-8d5e93e9afaa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cot}⁡({x}^{2})+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-13464/selection/9ef4a76e376a3d4b7dc5c7415fbf2a83901e6244035f7170ce282749faf1d280" :answer/id #uuid "1d65046c-a697-5d13-b533-7c7c384f5ce2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cot}⁡({x}^{2})+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-13464/selection/f964e44ba5aaeb9c42a6a5b14569b99d32ad7824d0bdbbafc26c7c304bd07e10" :answer/id #uuid "996b1fa3-473e-56d9-b56b-b1ca91c58013" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡({x}^{2})+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-13464/selection/2e3aeac6fde3f3db5321c1ca4df0a38d2697e5b8b26681ce869e078668e425b2" :answer/id #uuid "8f247102-e776-55f3-8c48-50707e3ce329" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cot}⁡({x}^{2})+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-13464/selection/55fcbc01bc35d0c8e425f080d14479227fffaf26887975b6bb9f25f6a9661407" :answer/id #uuid "6ec19654-d246-51bb-9115-de759a2c4c3e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cot}⁡({x}^{2})+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-13464/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d04670c0-aeef-55ff-b651-762f4bef55d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-13464/selection/2e3aeac6fde3f3db5321c1ca4df0a38d2697e5b8b26681ce869e078668e425b2" :answer-field/choices ["q-13464/selection/745652f4c7afdd0c761deb3804adc7fde54e58f1dc166529b70f3c1c015c1c27" "q-13464/selection/9ef4a76e376a3d4b7dc5c7415fbf2a83901e6244035f7170ce282749faf1d280" "q-13464/selection/f964e44ba5aaeb9c42a6a5b14569b99d32ad7824d0bdbbafc26c7c304bd07e10" "q-13464/selection/2e3aeac6fde3f3db5321c1ca4df0a38d2697e5b8b26681ce869e078668e425b2" "q-13464/selection/55fcbc01bc35d0c8e425f080d14479227fffaf26887975b6bb9f25f6a9661407"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-13464" :question/id #uuid "b2552dc5-99aa-5d23-af8b-93fb475eed33" :question/math-academy-id "q-13464" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int x{csc}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u={x}^{2}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2x\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u=x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{csc}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {csc}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})\\cdot x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {csc}^{2}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int {csc}^{2}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cot}⁡u+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cot}⁡({x}^{2})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-13464/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d359337c-4ec2-5100-bdac-d0858619db3b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-13464"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-13533/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "6f9251f6-3ba2-566b-bb44-817097d20b5a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-13533/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer/id #uuid "47966173-94f2-57cc-a918-8add5b9c0dbf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-13533/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "8af228a3-fdfd-53f8-985f-8fcf70a68e43" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-13533/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "ca78ea78-ad41-5163-a53f-c1d86136f972" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-13533/selection/d278d4936eb1c69dc660a77f5f1c7b1eb5b4a4db4aee8a8ad2dc52aa3f827f2e" :answer/id #uuid "7f5d4463-48a3-5405-9e15-6c8ad81ae959" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-13533/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "dba54b9d-c3a7-597f-8162-bfdc70783b7b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-13533/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-13533/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-13533/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" "q-13533/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-13533/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-13533/selection/d278d4936eb1c69dc660a77f5f1c7b1eb5b4a4db4aee8a8ad2dc52aa3f827f2e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-13533" :question/id #uuid "e33aac6d-c12b-5a93-9e1e-b04561354815" :question/math-academy-id "q-13533" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\pi /2}}5x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=2{x}^{2}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4x\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u=x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt{\\pi /2}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\pi $ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\pi /2}}5x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\pi /2}}5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2{x}^{2})\\cdot x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }5\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}(0) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-13533/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d359337c-4ec2-5100-bdac-d0858619db3b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-13533"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-350203/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "52d1eb58-5926-5241-93eb-e8aa11ad7600" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-350203/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "eb98ddc0-864a-5063-8d20-c9a572909035" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-350203/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-350203/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-350203" :question/id #uuid "791c81b3-d8df-54fa-8893-accd7178980e" :question/math-academy-id "q-350203" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\sqrt{\\pi /12}}^{\\sqrt{\\pi /6}}12x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we let $u=6{x}^{2},$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=12x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=12x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $\\sqrt{\\pi /12}$ | $\\sqrt{\\pi /6}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\pi /2$ | $\\pi $ |\n\nUsing the above, we can rewrite the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{\\pi /12}}^{\\sqrt{\\pi /6}}12x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\sqrt{\\pi /12}}^{\\sqrt{\\pi /6}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6{x}^{2})\\cdot 12x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u)\\,{|}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =0-1 \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-350203/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d359337c-4ec2-5100-bdac-d0858619db3b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-350203"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-350887/field-1/872a4c25023a86fe6bc30478727b695d3bf50717a6c14b96a114d4885763eb88" :answer/id #uuid "e0892abf-f18d-50b0-9400-19b799bfd082" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\ln(4)-\\ln(3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-350887/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "e2770ca5-0f64-5e6b-9d33-6c7afcd06ce6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-350887/field-1/872a4c25023a86fe6bc30478727b695d3bf50717a6c14b96a114d4885763eb88" :answer-field/choices ["q-350887/field-1/872a4c25023a86fe6bc30478727b695d3bf50717a6c14b96a114d4885763eb88"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-350887" :question/id #uuid "d4245d1b-ea43-5712-83b8-544965e9daa0" :question/math-academy-id "q-350887" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)}{{sin}^{2}⁡(x)+3}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we let $u={sin}^{2}⁡(x)+3,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\pi /2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can rewrite the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)}{{sin}^{2}⁡(x)+3}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡(x)+3}\\cdot 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{4}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|\\,{|}_{3}^{4} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡4-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{4}{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-350887/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc24eade-1b3d-5672-88fd-0bb48b371509"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-350887"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-350901/field-1/6f395dc4e1162d17ca26cd0c95aae82299c9460409d0d0281f64ce5ed9fac463" :answer/id #uuid "27306d91-64bd-55c1-ac13-b345eeea365d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\ln(6)-\\ln(5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-350901/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "2fd95e72-5037-5f2b-aef4-5dd99ac7150b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-350901/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "3d40771b-259f-5872-819b-9d0b3486f7ae" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-350901/field-1/6f395dc4e1162d17ca26cd0c95aae82299c9460409d0d0281f64ce5ed9fac463" :answer-field/choices ["q-350901/field-1/6f395dc4e1162d17ca26cd0c95aae82299c9460409d0d0281f64ce5ed9fac463" "q-350901/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-350901" :question/id #uuid "31265c46-0cc2-5457-8780-81ed14552e3e" :question/math-academy-id "q-350901" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{24\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x){cos}^{2}⁡(x)}{8{cos}^{3}⁡(x)+5}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we let $u=8{cos}^{3}⁡(x)+5,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(8{cos}^{3}⁡(x)+5)=-24{cos}^{2}⁡(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).\n$$\n\nSo, differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-24{cos}^{2}⁡(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,⟹\\,-\\text{d}u=24\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x){cos}^{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $\\pi /3$ | $\\pi /2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $6$ | $5$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can rewrite the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{24\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x){cos}^{2}⁡(x)}{8{cos}^{3}⁡(x)+5}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1}{8{cos}^{3}⁡(x)+5}\\cdot 24\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x){cos}^{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{6}^{5}\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot (-\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{6}^{5}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|{|}_{6}^{5} \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡6) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{6}{5})\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-350901/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc24eade-1b3d-5672-88fd-0bb48b371509"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-350901"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73674/selection/8fa1dfd1e968a82c872982c229865825a4abf219875175e92a3a7fbfce2c19b6" :answer/id #uuid "7339e952-ee52-5f8c-a9c0-b532b11fefbc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73674/selection/de4ad0f1c057a1b2d37a91dc7fd4e4311bf099a626e3ff4bc9e5c33771cd4050" :answer/id #uuid "0ff91919-aa30-5a15-aaef-a8988ebad7a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2})|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73674/selection/692b9fa40092bfbdffc38dc9e3e45d622466cfe0d717ceff300e2bb476a1811d" :answer/id #uuid "d4672362-570f-5a2f-904b-10c429d36621" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2})|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73674/selection/82641fe93de2f6aa77ca5b95e221f476d566f403e41ed979cb80fd5f6423fe62" :answer/id #uuid "c65b881d-b2f3-5877-9c9b-e740b5a15216" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2})|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73674/selection/d8d8d855be60e0f556461725682e738cf8a028b4f3e40ebe72b6de5ef485cf49" :answer/id #uuid "fbeaa44a-1ec4-59f7-a131-8fcf9c803f0e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73674/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fcfeac21-43df-5ab3-af65-347ae582c78d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73674/selection/8fa1dfd1e968a82c872982c229865825a4abf219875175e92a3a7fbfce2c19b6" :answer-field/choices ["q-73674/selection/8fa1dfd1e968a82c872982c229865825a4abf219875175e92a3a7fbfce2c19b6" "q-73674/selection/de4ad0f1c057a1b2d37a91dc7fd4e4311bf099a626e3ff4bc9e5c33771cd4050" "q-73674/selection/692b9fa40092bfbdffc38dc9e3e45d622466cfe0d717ceff300e2bb476a1811d" "q-73674/selection/82641fe93de2f6aa77ca5b95e221f476d566f403e41ed979cb80fd5f6423fe62" "q-73674/selection/d8d8d855be60e0f556461725682e738cf8a028b4f3e40ebe72b6de5ef485cf49"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73674" :question/id #uuid "6a0d0966-5b44-5ba8-a2dd-7a4e1c591c3b" :question/math-academy-id "q-73674" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\int \\frac{y\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2})}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}y.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the numerator is proportional to the derivative of the denominator, because\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2}))=2y\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2}).\n$$\n\nSo, let $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2}).$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}y}=2y\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2})\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{y\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2})}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})}\\cdot (y\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2}))\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-73674/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc24eade-1b3d-5672-88fd-0bb48b371509"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73674"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-350904/field-1/872a4c25023a86fe6bc30478727b695d3bf50717a6c14b96a114d4885763eb88" :answer/id #uuid "95d4c15b-d981-5e38-98d1-c60f45adc960" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\ln(4)-\\ln(3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-350904/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "82469416-052c-55b9-9527-ee8b620c1ba4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-350904/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ac978f2e-4585-5458-89bc-f74c77e4aef4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-350904/field-1/872a4c25023a86fe6bc30478727b695d3bf50717a6c14b96a114d4885763eb88" :answer-field/choices ["q-350904/field-1/872a4c25023a86fe6bc30478727b695d3bf50717a6c14b96a114d4885763eb88" "q-350904/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-350904" :question/id #uuid "7392953b-370c-5ac1-9356-c75a7236a22c" :question/math-academy-id "q-350904" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x)}{2+\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we let $u=2+\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x),$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x)\\,⟹\\,-\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $\\pi /6$ | $\\pi /2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $4$ | $3$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can rewrite the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x)}{2+\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1}{2+\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)}\\cdot (\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{4}^{3}\\frac{1}{u}\\,(-\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{4}^{3}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|{|}_{4}^{3} \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{4}{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-350904/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc24eade-1b3d-5672-88fd-0bb48b371509"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-350904"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-113998/selection/0a1e439db45f66f88b8f51a2fc97f01ef26f64b0dea0900086f119fe2fe22bf4" :answer/id #uuid "2fdee2a0-aa8a-5f9a-a015-05a476fd9c35" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+2|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113998/selection/4c2e581500f3a76f6523890ce62f91be9e40f50d7ec14c55b30a49a99a580919" :answer/id #uuid "3ccc9c94-0a0a-5314-a420-a03c44a05fb4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+2|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113998/selection/08aba97893e69f711736352d973240a7122f78ba4867603929e543142e4e6bc0" :answer/id #uuid "e47264a5-3d24-5bbe-b1c4-340691728a6b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+2|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113998/selection/f8ebc1f62636d2c67b4cdaed1fb08fe49962dada38cdb344fa0b873c6b398d84" :answer/id #uuid "9e2a8883-3df3-582c-b23a-530b452170b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{csc}⁡x|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113998/selection/157cc5b4679af9f71afe20038191398bf1f81408c51254ddd0a1b124175845dd" :answer/id #uuid "773c3166-c591-50f9-94fd-9d45b6fea28a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{csc}⁡x|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113998/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2b749213-8398-5e3a-988f-e62395b02832" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-113998/selection/08aba97893e69f711736352d973240a7122f78ba4867603929e543142e4e6bc0" :answer-field/choices ["q-113998/selection/0a1e439db45f66f88b8f51a2fc97f01ef26f64b0dea0900086f119fe2fe22bf4" "q-113998/selection/4c2e581500f3a76f6523890ce62f91be9e40f50d7ec14c55b30a49a99a580919" "q-113998/selection/08aba97893e69f711736352d973240a7122f78ba4867603929e543142e4e6bc0" "q-113998/selection/f8ebc1f62636d2c67b4cdaed1fb08fe49962dada38cdb344fa0b873c6b398d84" "q-113998/selection/157cc5b4679af9f71afe20038191398bf1f81408c51254ddd0a1b124175845dd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-113998" :question/id #uuid "15f12574-67f3-52fd-b2b8-cf7106b117cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-113998" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+2}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+2.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,⟹\\,-\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+2}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+2}\\cdot \\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot (-\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =-2\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+2|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-113998/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc24eade-1b3d-5672-88fd-0bb48b371509"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-113998"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-464"] :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle\\int 2 \\sin {\\left(\\dfrac x 3\\right)} \\,  \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "If we let $u=\\dfrac x 3,$ then\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = \\dfrac 1 3\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm d x =3\\, \\textrm d u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡u+C \\\\  & =-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-465"] :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle\\int 5 \\csc {\\left(6x+\\dfrac \\pi 3\\right)} \\cot {\\left(6x+\\dfrac \\pi 3\\right)} \\,  \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "If we let $u=6x+\\dfrac \\pi 3,$ then\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = 6\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm d x =\\dfrac 1 6\\, \\textrm d u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 5\\operatorname{csc}⁡(6x+\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\operatorname{cot}⁡(6x+\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\,\\text{d}x & =5\\int \\operatorname{csc}⁡(6x+\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\operatorname{cot}⁡(6x+\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5\\int \\operatorname{csc}⁡u\\operatorname{cot}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{6}\\int \\operatorname{csc}⁡u\\operatorname{cot}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{6}\\operatorname{csc}⁡u+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{6}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(6x+\\frac{\\pi }{3})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-466"] :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int x^2 \\sec^2\\left(x^3-\\dfrac{\\pi}{6}\\right)\\,\\textrm d x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u = x^3 - \\dfrac{\\pi}{6}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d} u}{\\textrm{d}x } = 3x^2 \\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\dfrac 1 3 \\textrm d u = x^2\\,\\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{2}{sec}^{2}⁡({x}^{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡({x}^{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\cdot {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡(u)\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int {sec}^{2}⁡(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡({x}^{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{6})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-467"] :question/problem "Evaluate the integral $\\displaystyle \\int_0^{\\pi/4} \\dfrac{\\tan x \\sec^2 x}{1+\\tan^2x}\\,\\textrm d x.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the numerator is proportional to the derivative of the denominator, because\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm d x}(1+\\tan^2 x) = 2\\tan{x}\\sec^2 x.\n$$\n\nSo, let $u = 1+\\tan^2 x.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d} u}{\\textrm{d}x } = 2\\tan x\\sec^2 x \\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\dfrac 1 2 \\textrm d u = \\tan x\\sec^2 x\\,\\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\pi/4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x{sec}^{2}⁡x}{1+{tan}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{1+{tan}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡x{sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
